Subject: [PATCH 03939/11362] [outer-loop] fix truncated exp4716 test poisoning
 the conductor pre-test gate (SKIP cascade)

The A4 task shipped tests/python/test_experiment_4716_..._readiness.py TRUNCATED:
the file ended mid-statement at `path.parent.mk` (AttributeError: 'PosixPath' has no
attribute 'mk'), so test_req_capstone_4716_loaders_and_fallback_extractors FAILED ->
poisoned the conductor's smart-subset pre-test gate -> EVERY .434 B/C task SKIPped
3x ("Pre-tests failing", self-heal aborted), 0 commits/hour. The 2026-06-10
agent-shipped-test-bug pattern. The implementation is correct; completed the
truncated test body to actually run+assert: write the 3 v434 lever payloads, assert
load_v434_lever_inputs reads all 3 (exists+sha256, correct experiment/config), and
assert the fallback extractors (_extract_first_win_rate/_ci_lower/_multi_level_deepen_
rate) on known shapes. 11/11 pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
